Now Pantheon can eventually learn things like:

For temporal problems, timeline → causal graph has high yield.

For ambiguous language, surface wording → etymological decomposition → relational graph has high yield.

For software architecture, prose → state machine → executable pseudocode has high yield.

For stuck problems, current representation → ∅ → independent reconstruction has high yield.

That last one reveals something important:

ZPC may be an extreme Re-Mark

Ordinary Re-Mark:

R_A(X)\rightarrow R_B(X)

Zero-crossing:

R_A(X)\rightarrow\varnothing_I\rightarrow R_B(X)

where I is the minimal invariant retained across the representational release.

